>Campfire extinguishing quick card
Stop adding fuel early. Keep enough water to put it out.
From a safe position wet the remains, stir to uncover embers, and wet again. Beware steam. Repeat until cold throughout. Check the edges for heat, smoke or glowing material without touching ash. Do not bury hot embers. If fire spreads, get away and call emergency services when possible.

